CH3_DATA = {'chapter_number': 'THREE', 'chapter_title': 'SYSTEM ANALYSIS AND DESIGN', 'sections': [{'num': '3.1', 'title': 'Software Development Methodology', 'paragraphs': ['The engineering of HostelFix was conducted following an Applied Software Engineering Design Research methodology governed by the Agile Scrum framework. Traditional linear software development methodologies (such as the classical Waterfall model) require complete, frozen requirements upfront and defer software integration to the final project stages. In a sociotechnical environment such as a university residential campus, student living conditions, administrative policies, and artisan operational habits cannot be fully predicted through abstract theoretical analysis. Waterfall models carry high risks of building rigid, over-engineered software that users ultimately bypass.', 'Agile Scrum was strategically selected due to its core principles of iterative value delivery, rapid empirical feedback loops, continuous stakeholder collaboration, and flexibility in adapting to discovered real-world constraints. The development lifecycle was structured into five distinct two-week sprint cycles preceded by a sprint zero devoted to requirements discovery and architectural modeling:', '1. Sprint 0 (Weeks 1 - 4): Requirements Elicitation, Domain Modeling, and Architecture', 'During this foundational phase, empirical stakeholder interviews and observational workflow audits were conducted across Commonwealth Hall, Legon Hall, and Jean Nelson Aka Hall. Porters, maintenance supervisors, hall tutors, and resident students were engaged to document existing communication breakdowns. The key finding from this phase was that porters and artisans strongly resisted rigid multi-stage digital gates. This led directly to the formulation of Architectural Decision Record 001 (ADR 001), which simplified the issue lifecycle into a lightweight operational record. Initial UML diagrams, ERDs, RESTful API endpoint contracts, and database schemas were drafted.', '2. Sprint 1 (Weeks 5 - 8): Core Infrastructure, Security, and Authentication', 'Sprint 1 delivered the foundational full-stack scaffolding: Express 5 backend setup with TypeScript, MongoDB Atlas connection pooling, Mongoose model definitions, and the cryptographic dual-token authentication engine. Endpoints for user login, token refresh, and logout were implemented alongside HTTP-only cookie handlers and role-based authorization middleware.', '3. Sprint 2 (Weeks 9 - 12): Student Resident Subsystem and Media Pipeline', 'Sprint 2 focused on the student user experience. The Next.js 16 client was initialized with Tailwind CSS and responsive layout shells. The multi-step issue submission form was engineered, incorporating category selectors, floor/room inputs, and Cloudinary image upload dropzones. The student dashboard and filterable issue history queues were integrated with backend REST endpoints.', '4. Sprint 3 (Weeks 13 - 16): Hall Manager Triage and Assignment Subsystem', 'Sprint 3 delivered the hall management portal. Scoped authorization middleware was finalized to restrict hall managers strictly to their assigned halls. Triage queues, issue acknowledgement actions, rejection dialogs with mandatory reason fields, and internal artisan assignment modals were implemented. Real-time status badges and timeline history logs were added.', '5. Sprint 4 (Weeks 17 - 20): Maintenance Work Orders, Dispute Window, and Background Daemons', "Sprint 4 established the maintenance staff portal, allowing artisans to view assigned jobs, update status to 'In Progress', and mark issues as 'Resolved' with resolution notes and completion photos. The resident dispute re-opening feature was engineered with a configurable 48-hour dispute window. Automated background daemons using node-cron were deployed to escalate overdue SLA tickets and auto-close resolved tickets.", '6. Sprint 5 (Weeks 21 - 24): Executive Analytics, Administration, and System Hardening', 'The final sprint implemented the University Administrator executive dashboard featuring cross-hall KPI comparisons, Mean Time to Repair (MTTR) analytics, and CSV export. The System Administrator console for user role assignment and hall provisioning was completed. Rigorous testing (Jest, Supertest, Playwright), security audits (Snyk, OWASP Top 10), and empirical User Acceptance Testing were conducted.', 'Definition of Done (DoD): To maintain rigorous engineering standards, each user story had to satisfy strict completion criteria before being accepted into the codebase: (a) 100% TypeScript type safety with zero compilation errors; (b) complete unit and integration test coverage for all new API routes; (c) adherence to Snyk static code security analysis with zero high-severity vulnerabilities; (d) verified mobile responsiveness across standard viewports; and (e) formal peer review and supervisor validation.']}, {'num': '3.2', 'title': 'Requirements Engineering', 'paragraphs': ['Requirements engineering began with an exhaustive stakeholder persona analysis to identify the operational goals, pain points, and technical capabilities of the diverse user groups interacting with the system:', 'Persona 1: Student Resident (Kofi, Age 20, 2nd Year Undergraduate, Commonwealth Hall). Tech-savvy, mobile-first user. Frustrated by broken louvers and leaking taps. Needs an intuitive, zero-training reporting interface that provides verifiable acknowledgement, real-time status visibility, and the power to dispute incomplete repairs.', 'Persona 2: Hall Manager (Mrs. Mensah, Age 48, Hall Administrator, Legon Hall). Desktop-oriented administrator managing high-volume operations. Overwhelmed by disorganized paper ledgers and chaotic WhatsApp complaints. Needs a consolidated, filterable triage queue to acknowledge valid issues, assign artisans, monitor hall repair backlogs, and generate hall council reports.', 'Persona 3: Maintenance Staff / Artisan (Master Kwesi, Age 42, Hall Plumber). Practical field worker with basic smartphone literacy. Dislikes complex data entry. Needs a simple, uncluttered list of assigned work orders with clear room locations, resident descriptions, and a one-click button to record repair completion.', 'Persona 4: University Administrator (Dr. Osei, Director of PDMSD). Executive decision-maker. Lacks visibility into campus-wide facility performance. Needs macro-level dashboards, cross-hall response time benchmarks, recurring trade defect analytics, and institutional accountability metrics to guide capital budget allocations.', 'Persona 5: System Administrator (Emmanuel, Directorate of ICT). IT operations specialist. Focuses on security, role provisioning, tenant isolation, uptime, and system integrity. Needs administrative tools to manage users, assign hall roles, monitor audit logs, and configure system parameters.', 'Based on this stakeholder analysis, thirty-five detailed functional requirements (FR) and twenty non-functional requirements (NFR) were elicited, analyzed, and categorized.'], 'functional_requirements_table': {'caption': 'Table 3.1: Comprehensive Functional Requirements Specification (FR-01 to FR-30)', 'headers': ['Req ID', 'Subsystem / Domain', 'User Role', 'Functional Requirement Description', 'Priority'], 'rows': [['FR-01', 'Authentication', 'All Users', 'The system shall authenticate users via unique institutional ID and password/PIN credentials.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-02', 'Authentication', 'All Users', 'The system shall issue short-lived JWT access tokens and secure HTTP-only refresh tokens upon valid login.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-03', 'Authentication', 'All Users', 'The system shall automatically refresh expired access tokens using rotation to prevent replay attacks.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-04', 'Authentication', 'All Users', 'The system shall invalidate refresh tokens in the database and clear cookies upon explicit logout.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-05', 'Issue Management', 'Student', 'The system shall enable students to submit maintenance tickets specifying category, location, and description.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-06', 'Issue Management', 'Student', 'The system shall allow students to upload photographic evidence directly via an integrated cloud CDN pipeline.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-07', 'Issue Management', 'Student', 'The system shall restrict students to viewing, tracking, and disputing only their own submitted issues.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-08', 'Issue Management', 'Student', 'The system shall allow students to reopen a resolved ticket within a 48-hour dispute window if repairs are defective.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-09', 'Triage & Workflow', 'Hall Manager', 'The system shall provide a real-time triage queue displaying all active maintenance tickets within the manager assigned hall.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-10', 'Triage & Workflow', 'Hall Manager', "The system shall allow hall managers to transition tickets from 'Submitted' to 'Acknowledged' to confirm awareness.", 'Must Have'], ['FR-11', 'Triage & Workflow', 'Hall Manager', 'The system shall allow hall managers to reject non-actionable or illegitimate tickets with a mandatory reason note.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-12', 'Assignment', 'Hall Manager', 'The system shall enable hall managers to assign an acknowledged ticket to a specific internal maintenance artisan.', 'Should Have'], ['FR-13', 'Maintenance', 'Maintenance Staff', 'The system shall provide artisans with a dedicated queue of work orders assigned to them within their designated hall.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-14', 'Maintenance', 'Maintenance Staff', "The system shall allow artisans to mark a work order as 'In Progress' to indicate physical repair commencement.", 'Could Have'], ['FR-15', 'Maintenance', 'Maintenance Staff', "The system shall allow artisans to transition a work order to 'Resolved', supplying resolution notes and completion photos.", 'Must Have'], ['FR-16', 'Notifications', 'All Users', 'The system shall generate contextual in-app notifications whenever a ticket status transitions or an assignment is made.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-17', 'Background Daemon', 'System / Cron', 'The system shall execute an automated daemon to identify tickets exceeding SLA limits and trigger overdue escalation.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-18', 'Background Daemon', 'System / Cron', "The system shall execute an automated daemon to transition 'Resolved' tickets to 'Closed' once the dispute window expires.", 'Must Have'], ['FR-19', 'Analytics', 'University Admin', 'The system shall provide executive dashboards aggregating cross-hall metrics, total tickets, and resolution rates.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-20', 'Analytics', 'University Admin', 'The system shall calculate and visualize Mean Time to Acknowledge (MTTA) and Mean Time to Repair (MTTR) by hall.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-21', 'Analytics', 'University Admin', 'The system shall generate distribution charts categorizing issues by technical trade (Plumbing, Electrical, Carpentry).', 'Should Have'], ['FR-22', 'Analytics', 'University Admin', 'The system shall support exporting filtered maintenance reporting data in standardized CSV format.', 'Should Have'], ['FR-23', 'Governance', 'System Admin', 'The system shall provide an administrative console to create, update, deactivate, and assign roles to user accounts.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-24', 'Governance', 'System Admin', 'The system shall allow administrators to provision and configure residential halls, blocks, and operational settings.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-25', 'Audit Logging', 'System Admin', 'The system shall record an immutable, timestamped audit log of all security, administrative, and status transition events.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-26', 'Security / RBAC', 'System', 'The system shall enforce strict object-level hall scoping, preventing hall managers from accessing tickets of other halls.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-27', 'Search & Filter', 'All Staff', 'The system shall support multi-parameter filtering of issue queues by status, trade category, priority, and date range.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-28', 'Timeline Tracking', 'All Users', 'The system shall display a chronological audit timeline for each ticket detailing every state transition and author.', 'Must Have'], ['FR-29', 'Profile Management', 'All Users', 'The system shall allow users to view and update their profile contact information and notification preferences.', 'Could Have'], ['FR-30', 'System Health', 'System Admin', 'The system shall expose a health check endpoint monitoring database connectivity, uptime, and memory consumption.', 'Must Have']]}, 'non_functional_requirements_table': {'caption': 'Table 3.2: Non-Functional Requirements Specification Mapped to ISO/IEC 25010 Quality Model', 'headers': ['NFR ID', 'Quality Characteristic', 'Metric / Specification', 'Verification Method'], 'rows': [['NFR-01', 'Performance Efficiency', 'API response time (p50) shall not exceed 100ms under standard operational loads.', 'Automated Autocannon load testing'], ['NFR-02', 'Performance Efficiency', 'API response time (p99) shall remain below 500ms under 100 concurrent requests.', 'Load benchmark simulation'], ['NFR-03', 'Performance Efficiency', 'Initial web page load (FCP) on 3G mobile connections shall occur within 2.5 seconds.', 'Google Lighthouse audit'], ['NFR-04', 'Security', 'All data in transit shall be encrypted using TLS 1.3 over HTTPS with HSTS enforcement.', 'SSL Labs cryptographic audit'], ['NFR-05', 'Security', 'All user passwords shall be hashed using bcrypt with a work factor of at least 10 rounds.', 'Static code & unit test verification'], ['NFR-06', 'Security', 'Access tokens shall expire after 15 minutes; refresh tokens stored in HTTP-only cookies.', 'Jest authentication suite'], ['NFR-07', 'Security', 'API shall enforce rate limiting (100 requests per 15-minute window per IP address).', 'Supertest rate limit integration test'], ['NFR-08', 'Security', 'All database queries shall use parameterized Mongoose schemas to eliminate NoSQL injection.', 'Snyk static security code analysis'], ['NFR-09', 'Reliability', 'The system shall maintain 99.5% operational uptime during standard academic semesters.', 'Synthetic uptime monitoring daemons'], ['NFR-10', 'Reliability', 'Database write operations shall enforce ACID properties and data validation constraints.', 'Database transaction test suites'], ['NFR-11', 'Usability', 'The application shall achieve a mean System Usability Scale (SUS) score of at least 75.', 'Empirical 42-participant UAT survey'], ['NFR-12', 'Usability', 'The user interface shall be fully responsive across mobile (375px), tablet, and desktop viewports.', 'Cross-browser responsive testing'], ['NFR-13', 'Maintainability', 'Backend codebase shall adhere to strict modular monolith architecture with zero circular dependencies.', 'TypeScript strict mode & ESLint'], ['NFR-14', 'Maintainability', 'API endpoints shall be documented using OpenAPI / Swagger 3.0 specifications.', 'Swagger UI automated generation'], ['NFR-15', 'Portability', 'The system shall be containerized using Docker and deployable across any Linux OS.', 'Docker container build verification']]}}, {'num': '3.3', 'title': 'Input Design', 'paragraphs': ['Input design is a critical aspect of user experience and system integrity. In a multi-user campus maintenance platform, poorly validated inputs lead to data corruption, security vulnerabilities (such as NoSQL injection and Cross-Site Scripting), and user frustration. HostelFix implements a defensive, multi-tier input validation architecture combining client-side schema validation (using Zod in Next.js) with strict server-side request payload sanitization (using Express-Validator and Mongoose schema constraints).', 'The system incorporates four primary data capture interfaces:', '1. User Authentication Form: Captures institutional User ID (student index number or staff ID) and secret password/PIN. Input fields enforce strict trimming, length boundaries, and masking.', '2. Student Issue Reporting Form: Captures fault category (Plumbing, Electrical, Carpentry, Masonry, Other), physical location details (Hall, Block, Floor, Room Number), issue title, narrative description, priority level, and multimedia image attachments. Image uploads are restricted to JPEG, PNG, and WebP formats with a strict 5MB per-file ceiling.', '3. Hall Manager Triage and Assignment Form: Captures administrative decisions on submitted tickets, including status transition commands (Acknowledge, Reject), mandatory rejection rationale notes, and artisan assignment selections.', '4. Maintenance Work Order Resolution Form: Captures repair completion summaries, labor/materials notes, and optional post-repair verification photographs.'], 'input_specifications_table': {'caption': 'Table 3.3: Detailed Input Data Specifications and Validation Rules', 'headers': ['Field Name', 'Interface Form', 'Data Type', 'UI Control Element', 'Validation Rules & Constraints'], 'rows': [['identifier', 'Login Form', 'String', 'Text Input', 'Required, Alphanumeric, 4 to 20 chars, trimmed, SQL/NoSQL sanitized'], ['password', 'Login Form', 'String', 'Password Input', 'Required, Min 6 chars, Max 128 chars, masked input'], ['title', 'Issue Report Form', 'String', 'Text Input', 'Required, Min 5 chars, Max 100 chars, special chars escaped'], ['category', 'Issue Report Form', 'Enum', 'Dropdown Select', 'Required, Must be one of: plumbing, electrical, carpentry, masonry, other'], ['location.block', 'Issue Report Form', 'String', 'Text Input', 'Required, Min 1 char, Max 30 chars, alphanumeric'], ['location.floor', 'Issue Report Form', 'String', 'Text Input', "Required, Min 1 char, Max 20 chars (e.g., '2nd Floor')"], ['location.room', 'Issue Report Form', 'String', 'Text Input', "Required, Min 1 char, Max 20 chars (e.g., 'Room 412')"], ['description', 'Issue Report Form', 'String', 'Textarea', 'Required, Min 10 chars, Max 2000 chars, whitespace trimmed'], ['priority', 'Issue Report Form', 'Enum', 'Radio / Select', 'Required, Must be one of: low, medium, high, urgent. Default: medium'], ['images', 'Issue Report Form', 'Array[File]', 'Drag-and-Drop Zone', 'Optional, Max 3 files, Max 5MB each, MIME: image/jpeg, image/png, image/webp'], ['rejectionReason', 'Manager Triage', 'String', 'Textarea', 'Required if status is REJECTED, Min 5 chars, Max 500 chars'], ['artisanId', 'Manager Assign', 'ObjectID', 'Select Dropdown', 'Required for assignment, Must be valid active User with role: maintenance'], ['resolutionNotes', 'Artisan Resolve', 'String', 'Textarea', 'Required for resolution, Min 5 chars, Max 1000 chars'], ['completionPhoto', 'Artisan Resolve', 'File', 'File Input', 'Optional, Max 5MB, MIME: image/jpeg, image/png, image/webp']]}}, {'num': '3.4', 'title': 'Output Design', 'paragraphs': ['Output design in HostelFix focuses on delivering clear, actionable, and role-tailored information that minimizes cognitive load and enhances operational visibility. The system provides visual, tabular, and automated notification outputs across all stakeholder workflows:', '1. Role-Adaptive Graphical Dashboards: Upon authentication, users are routed to a consolidated `/dashboard` endpoint that renders distinct views based on their institutional role. Student dashboards emphasize active ticket status cards and quick submission triggers. Hall manager dashboards emphasize triage counters (Pending Acknowledgment, In Progress, Overdue) and action-required queues. Maintenance dashboards present assigned task lists with room locations and contact links. University administrator dashboards present macro-level KPI cards and cross-hall comparative charts.', '2. Interactive Status Banners and Color-Coded Badges: To ensure instant comprehension of ticket states, HostelFix uses a standardized, high-contrast badge hierarchy: SUBMITTED (Blue / Info), ACKNOWLEDGED (Teal / Recognized), IN_PROGRESS (Purple / Active), RESOLVED (Amber / Warning - Pending Dispute Window), CLOSED (Green / Success), and REJECTED (Red / Danger).', "3. Chronological Audit Timeline Outputs: Every ticket detail page renders an event-sourced timeline showing the complete history from initial submission to final closure. Each timeline node displays the state transition, the user who triggered the change, their institutional role, a relative time indicator (e.g., '2 hours ago'), an ISO timestamp, and any contextual remarks.", '4. Automated In-App Notifications: The system generates contextual notification banners and alert counters whenever critical lifecycle events occur (e.g., when a student ticket is acknowledged or resolved, or when an artisan receives a new assignment).', '5. Analytical Reports and Data Export: University administrators can view real-time graphical outputs (Mean Time to Repair bar charts, trade category distribution donuts) and trigger on-demand CSV data exports containing filtered ticket records for institutional reporting.']}, {'num': '3.5', 'title': 'Database Design', 'paragraphs': ['The database tier of HostelFix is engineered using MongoDB, a high-performance document database, accessed through Mongoose Object Document Mapper (ODM). The database schema design balances document embedding (for tightly coupled, high-read data like location details and media URLs) with normalized referencing (for independent entities like Users, Residences, and Audit Logs).', '1. Conceptual and Logical Data Modeling: The conceptual model centers on the `Issue` aggregate, which references a `User` (reporter), a `Residence` (hall), and optionally an assigned `User` (artisan). To ensure an immutable historical record, all status mutations generate corresponding documents in the `issue_events` collection. Cross-hall administrative actions produce records in `audit_logs`. Cryptographic authentication is secured through the `refresh_tokens` collection featuring automated TTL expiration.', '2. Normalization Analysis: In traditional relational database design, data is normalized to Third Normal Form (3NF) to eliminate update anomalies. In document databases, strict normalization can lead to excessive application-level joins. HostelFix adopts a balanced approach: User identity, Hall definitions, and Issue records are normalized into separate collections to preserve entity independence. Conversely, immutable historical snapshots (such as reporter name and hall code at the moment of issue creation) are denormalized into issue events to guarantee that historical audit trails remain valid even if user profiles change.', "3. Indexing Strategy: To guarantee sub-millisecond query execution across thousands of documents, MongoDB compound and specialized indexes are implemented: (a) Compound index on `{ residence: 1, status: 1, createdAt: -1 }` on the `issues` collection for ultra-fast hall manager queue filtering; (b) Index on `{ reporter: 1, createdAt: -1 }` for instant student history retrieval; (c) TTL index on `{ expiresAt: 1 }` with `expireAfterSeconds: 0` on `refresh_tokens` for automated session cleanup; and (d) Text search index on `{ title: 'text', description: 'text' }` for keyword querying."], 'data_dictionaries': [{'table_name': 'users', 'caption': "Table 3.4: Data Dictionary for 'users' Collection", 'headers': ['Field Name', 'BSON Data Type', 'Constraints / Key', 'Description & Business Rules'], 'rows': [['_id', 'ObjectId', 'Primary Key, Auto', 'Unique immutable internal identifier for the user account'], ['identifier', 'String', 'Unique, Required, Index', 'Institutional student index number or staff ID number'], ['name', 'String', 'Required, Trimmed', 'Full official legal name of the user'], ['email', 'String', 'Unique, Required, Index', 'Official institutional or personal email address'], ['phone', 'String', 'Optional, Trimmed', 'Mobile telephone contact number for SMS and direct calls'], ['passwordHash', 'String', 'Required', 'Bcrypt cryptographic hash of the user password/PIN (cost 10)'], ['role', 'String', 'Required, Enum', "User role: 'student', 'hall_manager', 'maintenance', 'university_admin', 'system_admin'"], ['residence', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> residences', 'Assigned hall of residence (Required for students, managers, artisans)'], ['room', 'String', 'Optional, Trimmed', 'Default residential room number for student residents'], ['trade', 'String', 'Optional, Enum', "Specialization for artisans: 'plumbing', 'electrical', 'carpentry', 'masonry', 'other'"], ['isActive', 'Boolean', 'Required, Default: true', 'Account activation flag; false disables login'], ['createdAt', 'Date', 'Auto, Timestamp', 'Timestamp of account creation in ISO format'], ['updatedAt', 'Date', 'Auto, Timestamp', 'Timestamp of most recent account modification']]}, {'table_name': 'issues', 'caption': "Table 3.5: Data Dictionary for 'issues' Collection", 'headers': ['Field Name', 'BSON Data Type', 'Constraints / Key', 'Description & Business Rules'], 'rows': [['_id', 'ObjectId', 'Primary Key, Auto', 'Unique immutable internal identifier for the maintenance issue'], ['ticketNumber', 'String', 'Unique, Required, Index', "Human-readable sequential tracking code (e.g., 'HF-2026-0042')"], ['title', 'String', 'Required, Max 100', 'Concise summary title of the reported maintenance defect'], ['description', 'String', 'Required, Max 2000', 'Comprehensive textual description of the fault and symptoms'], ['category', 'String', 'Required, Enum, Index', "Trade category: 'plumbing', 'electrical', 'carpentry', 'masonry', 'other'"], ['priority', 'String', 'Required, Enum', "Urgency level: 'low', 'medium', 'high', 'urgent'. Default: 'medium'"], ['status', 'String', 'Required, Enum, Index', "State: 'submitted', 'acknowledged', 'in_progress', 'resolved', 'closed', 'rejected', 'reopened'"], ['residence', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> residences', 'Residential hall where the fault is physically located'], ['location.block', 'String', 'Required, Trimmed', 'Specific hall residential block, wing, or annex name'], ['location.floor', 'String', 'Required, Trimmed', "Floor level identification (e.g., 'Ground Floor', '3rd Floor')"], ['location.room', 'String', 'Required, Trimmed', 'Specific room number or communal facility description'], ['reporter', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> users', 'Reference to the student resident who created the report'], ['assignedTo', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> users, Null', 'Reference to the assigned maintenance technician / artisan'], ['images', 'Array[String]', 'Max 3 items', 'Array of secure HTTPS image URLs hosted on Cloudinary CDN'], ['rejectionReason', 'String', 'Optional, Max 500', 'Mandatory explanation note if the ticket was rejected'], ['resolutionNotes', 'String', 'Optional, Max 1000', 'Technical summary of repair actions executed by the artisan'], ['resolvedAt', 'Date', 'Optional, Nullable', 'Timestamp when ticket was marked resolved (starts dispute timer)'], ['disputeWindowClosesAt', 'Date', 'Optional, Nullable', 'Timestamp when the 48-hour student dispute window lapses'], ['closedAt', 'Date', 'Optional, Nullable', 'Timestamp when ticket entered final closed state'], ['createdAt', 'Date', 'Auto, Timestamp, Index', 'Timestamp of initial issue creation'], ['updatedAt', 'Date', 'Auto, Timestamp', 'Timestamp of most recent issue modification']]}, {'table_name': 'issue_events', 'caption': "Table 3.6: Data Dictionary for 'issue_events' Collection (Audit Trail)", 'headers': ['Field Name', 'BSON Data Type', 'Constraints / Key', 'Description & Business Rules'], 'rows': [['_id', 'ObjectId', 'Primary Key, Auto', 'Unique identifier for the lifecycle event record'], ['issue', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> issues, Index', 'Reference to the parent issue ticket'], ['eventType', 'String', 'Required, Enum', "Event type: 'CREATED', 'ACKNOWLEDGED', 'ASSIGNED', 'IN_PROGRESS', 'RESOLVED', 'REOPENED', 'CLOSED', 'REJECTED'"], ['previousStatus', 'String', 'Optional, Enum', 'Lifecycle state immediately prior to this transition event'], ['newStatus', 'String', 'Required, Enum', 'Lifecycle state resulting from this transition event'], ['triggeredBy', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> users', 'Reference to the authenticated user who initiated the event'], ['notes', 'String', 'Optional, Trimmed', 'Contextual remarks, rejection reason, or resolution details'], ['metadata', 'Object', 'Optional', 'Arbitrary JSON payload capturing IP address, user agent, or artisan ID'], ['createdAt', 'Date', 'Auto, Timestamp, Index', 'High-precision immutable timestamp of event occurrence']]}, {'table_name': 'residences', 'caption': "Table 3.7: Data Dictionary for 'residences' Collection (Halls of Residence)", 'headers': ['Field Name', 'BSON Data Type', 'Constraints / Key', 'Description & Business Rules'], 'rows': [['_id', 'ObjectId', 'Primary Key, Auto', 'Unique identifier for the residential hall entity'], ['name', 'String', 'Unique, Required', "Official name (e.g., 'Commonwealth Hall', 'Legon Hall')"], ['code', 'String', 'Unique, Required, Index', "Standard short code (e.g., 'CW', 'LH', 'MSH', 'JN', 'AK')"], ['category', 'String', 'Required, Enum', "Classification: 'traditional', 'diaspora', 'private_partner'"], ['capacity', 'Number', 'Required, Integer', 'Total resident bed capacity of the residential facility'], ['isActive', 'Boolean', 'Required, Default: true', 'Operational status flag of the residential hall'], ['createdAt', 'Date', 'Auto, Timestamp', 'Timestamp when hall was provisioned in the system']]}, {'table_name': 'refresh_tokens', 'caption': "Table 3.8: Data Dictionary for 'refresh_tokens' Collection", 'headers': ['Field Name', 'BSON Data Type', 'Constraints / Key', 'Description & Business Rules'], 'rows': [['_id', 'ObjectId', 'Primary Key, Auto', 'Unique identifier for the refresh token record'], ['tokenHash', 'String', 'Unique, Required, Index', 'Cryptographic SHA-256 hash of the opaque refresh token'], ['user', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> users, Index', 'Reference to the authenticated user owning this session'], ['expiresAt', 'Date', 'Required, TTL Index', 'Expiration timestamp (TTL index automatically deletes expired documents)'], ['isRevoked', 'Boolean', 'Required, Default: false', 'Revocation flag set upon explicit logout or replay detection'], ['userAgent', 'String', 'Optional, Trimmed', 'Client browser user-agent string for session auditing'], ['ipAddress', 'String', 'Optional, Trimmed', 'Client remote IP address recorded during token generation']]}, {'table_name': 'assignments', 'caption': 'Table 3.9: Data Dictionary for assignments Collection', 'headers': ['Field Name', 'BSON Data Type', 'Constraints / Key', 'Description & Business Rules'], 'rows': [['_id', 'ObjectId', 'Primary Key, Auto', 'Unique identifier for the work order assignment record'], ['issue', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> issues, Index', 'Reference to the maintenance ticket being assigned'], ['artisan', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> users, Index', 'Reference to the maintenance staff assigned to execute repair'], ['assignedBy', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> users', 'Reference to the hall manager who issued the assignment'], ['instructions', 'String', 'Optional, Max 500', 'Specific instructions, safety notes, or tool requirements from manager'], ['status', 'String', 'Required, Enum', 'Assignment state: active, completed, reassigned, cancelled'], ['assignedAt', 'Date', 'Auto, Timestamp, Index', 'Timestamp when the work order assignment was formalized'], ['completedAt', 'Date', 'Optional, Nullable', 'Timestamp when the artisan completed the assigned physical work']]}, {'table_name': 'notifications', 'caption': 'Table 3.10: Data Dictionary for notifications Collection', 'headers': ['Field Name', 'BSON Data Type', 'Constraints / Key', 'Description & Business Rules'], 'rows': [['_id', 'ObjectId', 'Primary Key, Auto', 'Unique identifier for the notification document'], ['recipient', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> users, Index', 'User receiving the notification alert'], ['issue', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> issues, Optional', 'Associated maintenance ticket triggering the notification'], ['type', 'String', 'Required, Enum', 'Category: ISSUE_STATUS_CHANGE, ISSUE_ASSIGNED, DISPUTE_ALERT, SLA_OVERDUE'], ['title', 'String', 'Required, Max 100', 'Concise notification header displayed in UI banner'], ['message', 'String', 'Required, Max 500', 'Full descriptive message explaining the event and context'], ['isRead', 'Boolean', 'Required, Default: false, Index', 'Flag indicating whether the recipient has viewed the alert'], ['readAt', 'Date', 'Optional, Nullable', 'Timestamp when recipient clicked or marked the alert as read'], ['createdAt', 'Date', 'Auto, Timestamp, Index', 'Timestamp of notification dispatch']]}, {'table_name': 'audit_logs', 'caption': 'Table 3.11: Data Dictionary for audit_logs Collection', 'headers': ['Field Name', 'BSON Data Type', 'Constraints / Key', 'Description & Business Rules'], 'rows': [['_id', 'ObjectId', 'Primary Key, Auto', 'Unique identifier for the system audit record'], ['actor', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> users, Index', 'User initiating the security or administrative transaction'], ['action', 'String', 'Required, Enum, Index', 'Action: USER_LOGIN, USER_LOGOUT, USER_CREATE, USER_ROLE_CHANGE, HALL_CREATE, SYSTEM_PARAM_UPDATE'], ['entityType', 'String', 'Required, Trimmed', 'Target domain entity: User, Residence, SystemSettings, Issue'], ['entityId', 'String', 'Optional, Trimmed', 'String representation of the target entity identifier'], ['details', 'Object', 'Required', 'JSON payload capturing before/after state diffs, IP address, user agent'], ['ipAddress', 'String', 'Optional, Trimmed', 'Client remote IPv4/IPv6 address recorded at request time'], ['createdAt', 'Date', 'Auto, Timestamp, Index', 'Immutable timestamp of audit log entry (TTL 365 days)']]}, {'table_name': 'system_settings', 'caption': 'Table 3.12: Data Dictionary for system_settings Collection', 'headers': ['Field Name', 'BSON Data Type', 'Constraints / Key', 'Description & Business Rules'], 'rows': [['_id', 'ObjectId', 'Primary Key, Auto', 'Unique identifier for the system configuration document'], ['key', 'String', 'Unique, Required, Index', 'Configuration setting key (e.g., SLA_URGENT_HOURS, DISPUTE_WINDOW_HOURS)'], ['value', 'Mixed', 'Required', 'Configured setting value (Number, String, Boolean, or JSON)'], ['description', 'String', 'Required, Trimmed', 'Human-readable explanation of the setting and operational impact'], ['updatedBy', 'ObjectId', 'Foreign Key -> users', 'System administrator who last modified the configuration'], ['updatedAt', 'Date', 'Auto, Timestamp', 'Timestamp of most recent configuration update']]}]}, {'num': '3.6', 'title': 'System Modeling and UML Diagrams', 'paragraphs': ['Unified Modeling Language (UML) provides a standardized visual specification language for modeling the structural, behavioral, and architectural dimensions of software systems. This section presents the comprehensive UML and architectural models governing HostelFix:', '3.6.1 System Architecture Diagram', 'HostelFix employs a Multi-Tier Modular Monolith architecture designed for high cohesion, low coupling, and operational maintainability. As illustrated in Figure 3.1, the system is organized into five distinct architectural tiers:', '1. Presentation Tier (Client): Built with Next.js 16, React 19, and Tailwind CSS. Renders responsive user interfaces across mobile and desktop browsers, handles client-side form validation, and manages access tokens in memory.', '2. Network and Routing Tier: Managed by an Nginx reverse proxy terminating TLS 1.3 encryption, enforcing HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS), and routing incoming traffic to application instances managed by PM2 cluster mode.', '3. API and Business Logic Tier: Built on Express 5 and TypeScript. Structured into modular domain packages (Auth, Issues, Assignments, Notifications, Analytics, Admin) communicating through well-defined service interfaces and policy gates.', '4. Persistence Tier: Powered by MongoDB Atlas utilizing replica sets, compound indexes, and ACID document transactions.', '5. External Cloud Services Tier: Integrates Cloudinary CDN for direct image transformations and optimization, and Node-cron for background task execution.'], 'figures': [{'id': 'fig_3_1', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_1_architecture.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.1: Multi-Tier Modular Monolith Architecture of the HostelFix Platform', 'description': 'Architectural block diagram showing Presentation, Routing, Modular API, Persistence, and Cloud Storage tiers.'}, {'id': 'fig_3_2', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_2_component_diagram.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.2: UML Component Diagram Illustrating Internal Modular Boundaries', 'description': 'Component diagram detailing Auth, Issues, Assignments, Notifications, Analytics, and Audit modules and their interfaces.'}, {'id': 'fig_3_13', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_13_network_topology.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.3: Physical Network Deployment and Infrastructure Topology Diagram', 'description': 'Network topology showing client requests routed through Nginx reverse proxy, Node.js cluster, MongoDB Atlas, and Cloudinary CDN.'}, {'id': 'fig_3_2_state', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_2_state_machine.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.4: Operational State Machine Diagram Governed by ADR 001', 'description': 'UML state machine illustrating transitions: Submitted, Acknowledged, In Progress, Resolved, Closed, Reopened, Rejected.'}, {'id': 'fig_3_3_erd', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_3_erd.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.5: Entity-Relationship Diagram (ERD) of the HostelFix Database', 'description': 'Comprehensive ERD showing Users, Issues, IssueEvents, Residences, Assignments, RefreshTokens, and Notifications.'}, {'id': 'fig_3_4_class', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_4_class_diagram.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.6: UML Domain Class Diagram Illustrating Model Classes and Associations', 'description': 'Class diagram showing attributes, methods, relationships, and multiplicities across core entities.'}, {'id': 'fig_3_3_uc', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_3_use_case_diagram.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.7: Comprehensive UML Use Case Diagram across Five Stakeholder Roles', 'description': 'Use case diagram depicting actor boundaries and interactions for Student, Hall Manager, Artisan, University Admin, and System Admin.'}, {'id': 'fig_3_6_seq_auth', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_6_sequence_auth_jwt.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.8: UML Sequence Diagram: Dual-Token JWT Authentication and Refresh Cycle', 'description': 'Sequence diagram showing client login, token dispatch, protected API query, token expiry, and cookie-based refresh.'}, {'id': 'fig_3_5_seq_issue', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_5_sequence_issue_lifecycle.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.9: UML Sequence Diagram: Complete Issue Reporting, Triage, and Resolution Lifecycle', 'description': 'Sequence diagram illustrating interactions between Student, Hall Manager, Maintenance Staff, API, and Database.'}, {'id': 'fig_3_8_flow_student', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_8_flowchart_student_reporting.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.10: Activity Flowchart: Student Incident Reporting and Validation Workflow', 'description': 'Flowchart detailing student navigation, input validation, image upload, ticket generation, and feedback.'}, {'id': 'fig_3_9_flow_mgr', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_9_flowchart_manager_triage.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.11: Activity Flowchart: Hall Manager Triage and Assignment Workflow', 'description': 'Flowchart showing manager ticket inspection, legitimacy check, acknowledgement, rejection, and artisan dispatch.'}, {'id': 'fig_3_10_flow_maint', 'path': 'docs/diagrams/fig_3_10_flowchart_maintenance_resolution.png', 'caption': 'Figure 3.12: Activity Flowchart: Maintenance Technician Work Order Execution and Resolution Workflow', 'description': 'Flowchart detailing work order pickup, in-progress logging, repair execution, resolution submission, and dispute timer.'}], 'use_case_specifications': [{'uc_id': 'UC-01', 'caption': 'Table 3.9: Use Case Specification UC-01: Authenticate with Credentials', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-01'], ['Use Case Name', 'Authenticate with Credentials'], ['Primary Actor', 'All Stakeholder Roles (Student, Hall Manager, Maintenance Staff, University Admin, System Admin)'], ['Preconditions', 'User must possess an active, non-deactivated institutional account in the database.'], ['Trigger', 'User navigates to the login screen (`/login`) and submits institutional ID and password/PIN.'], ['Main Success Scenario', '1. User enters institutional identifier and password credentials.\n2. System validates format and non-empty constraints.\n3. System queries user collection and compares password hash via bcrypt.\n4. System verifies account is active.\n5. System generates 15-minute JWT access token and cryptographic refresh token.\n6. System stores refresh token hash in database and attaches it to an HTTP-only, SameSite cookie.\n7. System returns user profile and access token in JSON response.\n8. Client redirects user to role-specific dashboard.'], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', '3a. User identifier not found: System returns 401 Unauthorized with error message.\n3b. Password mismatch: System returns 401 Unauthorized.\n4a. Account is deactivated (`isActive: false`): System returns 403 Forbidden with contact administrator notice.'], ['Postconditions', 'User is authenticated; cryptographic session established; access token stored in memory.']]}, {'uc_id': 'UC-02', 'caption': 'Table 3.10: Use Case Specification UC-02: Submit Maintenance Ticket', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-02'], ['Use Case Name', 'Submit Maintenance Ticket'], ['Primary Actor', 'Student Resident'], ['Preconditions', "Student must be authenticated with valid role 'student' and assigned to a residential hall."], ['Trigger', "Student clicks 'Report an Issue' on dashboard or navigates to `/issues/report`."], ['Main Success Scenario', "1. System presents multi-step ticket submission form.\n2. Student selects trade category (plumbing, electrical, carpentry, masonry, other).\n3. Student confirms or edits residential location details (Block, Floor, Room Number).\n4. Student inputs issue title and comprehensive description.\n5. Student selects priority level.\n6. Student optionally attaches up to 3 image files via drag-and-drop zone.\n7. Client validates files (JPEG/PNG/WebP, <=5MB) and uploads to Cloudinary CDN.\n8. Student clicks Submit Ticket.\n9. Backend validates payload via Express-Validator, creates Issue document (Status: SUBMITTED), creates initial IssueEvent, and dispatches in-app notification to hall manager.\n10. System displays confirmation banner with generated tracking ticket number (e.g., 'HF-2026-0042')."], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', '7a. File exceeds 5MB or invalid MIME type: Client displays immediate validation error and halts submission.\n9a. Validation failure on server: Backend returns 422 Unprocessable Entity with error fields.'], ['Postconditions', 'New Issue record persisted; Status is SUBMITTED; Hall manager queue updated.']]}, {'uc_id': 'UC-05', 'caption': 'Table 3.11: Use Case Specification UC-05: Acknowledge Submitted Ticket', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-05'], ['Use Case Name', 'Acknowledge Submitted Ticket (ADR 001)'], ['Primary Actor', 'Hall Manager'], ['Preconditions', 'Hall Manager is authenticated; issue belongs to manager assigned hall; issue status is SUBMITTED.'], ['Trigger', "Manager clicks 'Acknowledge' button on an unacknowledged ticket in the triage queue."], ['Main Success Scenario', "1. Manager inspects ticket details, description, and attached photos.\n2. Manager verifies the issue is legitimate and within the hall jurisdiction.\n3. Manager clicks 'Acknowledge' button.\n4. Backend validates authorization and transitions status from SUBMITTED to ACKNOWLEDGED.\n5. Backend appends an ACKNOWLEDGED event to the IssueEvent timeline.\n6. Backend dispatches real-time notification to reporting student.\n7. System refreshes triage queue; badge updates to Teal (Acknowledged)."], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', "2a. Issue is illegitimate or non-actionable: Manager clicks 'Reject', enters required reason note, and status transitions to REJECTED."], ['Postconditions', 'Issue status updated to ACKNOWLEDGED; institutional awareness officially recorded.']]}, {'uc_id': 'UC-07', 'caption': 'Table 3.12: Use Case Specification UC-07: Update Status to Resolved', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-07'], ['Use Case Name', 'Update Status to Resolved'], ['Primary Actor', 'Maintenance Staff / Artisan (or Hall Manager)'], ['Preconditions', 'User is authenticated; issue status is ACKNOWLEDGED or IN_PROGRESS.'], ['Trigger', "Artisan completes physical repair and clicks 'Mark Resolved' on the work order."], ['Main Success Scenario', "1. Artisan inspects assigned ticket details.\n2. Artisan clicks 'Mark Resolved'.\n3. System displays resolution dialog requesting resolution summary and optional completion photo.\n4. Artisan enters notes describing completed repair and optionally uploads photo.\n5. Backend updates issue status to RESOLVED, sets `resolvedAt` to current timestamp, and sets `disputeWindowClosesAt` to timestamp + 48 hours.\n6. Backend records RESOLVED event in IssueEvents.\n7. Backend dispatches resolution notification to student resident, alerting them that the 48-hour dispute window has commenced.\n8. System updates artisan queue; ticket moves to resolved archive."], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', '4a. Resolution notes empty: System displays validation error; notes are required.'], ['Postconditions', 'Issue status is RESOLVED; 48-hour dispute countdown timer active; student notified.']]}, {'uc_id': 'UC-04', 'caption': 'Table 3.13: Use Case Specification UC-04: Dispute Resolution (Reopen Ticket)', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-04'], ['Use Case Name', 'Dispute Resolution (Reopen Ticket)'], ['Primary Actor', 'Student Resident'], ['Preconditions', 'Student is authenticated; issue was submitted by student; status is RESOLVED; current time < `disputeWindowClosesAt`.'], ['Trigger', "Student observes repair was inadequate or defective and clicks 'Dispute / Reopen'."], ['Main Success Scenario', "1. Student navigates to ticket details page.\n2. System verifies dispute window is active and renders 'Dispute Resolution' button.\n3. Student clicks 'Dispute Resolution'.\n4. System displays modal requesting reason for dispute and counter-evidence.\n5. Student enters detailed dispute rationale and optionally attaches new photos.\n6. Backend transitions issue status from RESOLVED to REOPENED.\n7. Backend appends REOPENED event with dispute notes to IssueEvents.\n8. Backend dispatches high-priority notification to Hall Manager and assigned artisan.\n9. System updates ticket status badge to Amber/Red (Reopened); ticket returns to active triage queue."], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', '2a. Dispute window has expired: System hides dispute button; ticket has transitioned to CLOSED.'], ['Postconditions', 'Issue status is REOPENED; ticket returned to active queue; manager alerted to failure.']]}, {'uc_id': 'UC-03', 'caption': 'Table 3.13: Use Case Specification UC-03: View and Filter Personal Issue History', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-03'], ['Use Case Name', 'View and Filter Personal Issue History'], ['Primary Actor', 'Student Resident'], ['Preconditions', 'Student is authenticated with role student.'], ['Trigger', 'Student clicks My Issues in navigation or navigates to /issues.'], ['Main Success Scenario', '1. System fetches all issues where reporter matches current user ID.\n2. System renders tabular list sorted chronologically descending.\n3. Student applies filter by status (e.g., Acknowledged).\n4. System filters records in-memory or triggers API query.\n5. Student enters keyword in search input.\n6. System renders filtered results with status pills and ticket tracking numbers.'], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', '1a. No issues found: System renders informative empty state with Report an Issue button.'], ['Postconditions', 'Filtered issue list displayed to student; zero data from other students exposed.']]}, {'uc_id': 'UC-06', 'caption': 'Table 3.14: Use Case Specification UC-06: Reject Illegitimate Ticket with Reason', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-06'], ['Use Case Name', 'Reject Illegitimate Ticket with Reason'], ['Primary Actor', 'Hall Manager'], ['Preconditions', 'Hall Manager is authenticated; issue belongs to manager hall; status is SUBMITTED.'], ['Trigger', 'Manager inspects ticket and determines fault is non-actionable or private appliance.'], ['Main Success Scenario', '1. Manager clicks Reject button on ticket card.\n2. System renders rejection modal with required reason textarea.\n3. Manager enters clear justification note (e.g., Private appliance fault; personal repair required).\n4. Manager confirms rejection.\n5. Backend validates reason length (>= 5 chars), updates status to REJECTED, and logs IssueEvent.\n6. Backend dispatches notification to student with rejection explanation.\n7. Triage queue updates; badge transitions to Red (Rejected).'], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', '3a. Reason field empty: System prevents submission and displays validation alert.'], ['Postconditions', 'Ticket status updated to REJECTED; student notified of specific reason.']]}, {'uc_id': 'UC-08', 'caption': 'Table 3.15: Use Case Specification UC-08: Execute Repair and Update Status to In Progress', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-08'], ['Use Case Name', 'Execute Repair and Update Status to In Progress'], ['Primary Actor', 'Maintenance Staff / Artisan'], ['Preconditions', 'Artisan is authenticated; ticket is assigned to artisan or belongs to artisan hall.'], ['Trigger', 'Artisan arrives at physical repair site and begins technical maintenance.'], ['Main Success Scenario', '1. Artisan opens work order on mobile device.\n2. Artisan clicks Start Work / In Progress.\n3. Backend validates artisan role, transitions status to IN_PROGRESS, and logs IssueEvent.\n4. Backend dispatches real-time notification to reporting student and hall manager.\n5. UI status badge updates to Purple (In Progress).'], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', '2a. Artisan proceeds directly to repair without clicking In Progress: ADR 001 permits direct transition from ACKNOWLEDGED to RESOLVED.'], ['Postconditions', 'Ticket status updated to IN_PROGRESS; student informed that technician is actively on-site.']]}, {'uc_id': 'UC-09', 'caption': 'Table 3.16: Use Case Specification UC-09: Complete Work Order and Submit Resolution Evidence', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-09'], ['Use Case Name', 'Complete Work Order and Submit Resolution Evidence'], ['Primary Actor', 'Maintenance Staff / Artisan (or Hall Manager)'], ['Preconditions', 'Artisan has completed physical repair; ticket status is ACKNOWLEDGED or IN_PROGRESS.'], ['Trigger', 'Artisan clicks Mark Resolved.'], ['Main Success Scenario', '1. Artisan clicks Mark Resolved button.\n2. System presents resolution modal requesting summary of actions taken and optional proof photo.\n3. Artisan inputs notes (e.g., Replaced 1/2-inch brass ball valve; tested pressure; no leaks).\n4. Artisan optionally captures and attaches completion photo via mobile camera dropzone.\n5. System uploads photo to Cloudinary and submits resolution payload to backend.\n6. Backend transitions status to RESOLVED, sets resolvedAt, and starts 48-hour dispute timer.\n7. Backend dispatches resolution notification to student resident.\n8. Work order queue refreshes; ticket moves to resolved section.'], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', '3a. Resolution notes empty: System displays validation error; notes are required.'], ['Postconditions', 'Issue status is RESOLVED; 48-hour dispute window timer active; student alerted.']]}, {'uc_id': 'UC-10', 'caption': 'Table 3.17: Use Case Specification UC-10: View Cross-Hall Facility Analytics and MTTR', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-10'], ['Use Case Name', 'View Cross-Hall Facility Analytics and MTTR'], ['Primary Actor', 'University Administrator (PDMSD)'], ['Preconditions', 'User is authenticated with role university_admin or system_admin.'], ['Trigger', 'Administrator clicks Analytics in navigation or navigates to /analytics.'], ['Main Success Scenario', '1. System queries database and computes campus-wide aggregated metrics.\n2. System renders macro KPI cards: Total Campus Tickets, Resolution Rate, Mean MTTR, Overdue Tickets.\n3. System renders comparative horizontal bar chart ranking all halls by MTTR.\n4. System renders trade distribution donut chart (Plumbing, Electrical, Carpentry, Masonry).\n5. Administrator applies date range filter (e.g., Past 30 Days).\n6. System recalculates metrics and updates visual charts dynamically.'], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', '1a. Unauthorized role (e.g., Student or Hall Manager): Backend returns 403 Forbidden.'], ['Postconditions', 'Cross-hall facility intelligence displayed to executive leadership.']]}, {'uc_id': 'UC-11', 'caption': 'Table 3.18: Use Case Specification UC-11: Provision User Accounts and Assign Hall Roles', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-11'], ['Use Case Name', 'Provision User Accounts and Assign Hall Roles'], ['Primary Actor', 'System Administrator'], ['Preconditions', 'User is authenticated with role system_admin.'], ['Trigger', 'Administrator clicks User Management in admin console or navigates to /admin/users.'], ['Main Success Scenario', '1. System displays searchable user directory with role badges and active status.\n2. Administrator clicks Create User.\n3. Administrator enters User ID, legal name, email, role, and assigned hall of residence.\n4. Backend validates fields, generates initial PIN, hashes password via bcrypt, and creates User record.\n5. Backend logs USER_CREATE action in audit_logs collection.\n6. User directory refreshes showing new account with green Active badge.'], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', '4a. Duplicate User ID or Email: Backend returns 409 Conflict with field error.'], ['Postconditions', 'New institutional user account provisioned with enforced role and hall boundaries.']]}, {'uc_id': 'UC-12', 'caption': 'Table 3.19: Use Case Specification UC-12: Inspect System Audit Logs and Trigger Manual Escalation', 'rows': [['Use Case ID', 'UC-12'], ['Use Case Name', 'Inspect System Audit Logs and Trigger Manual Escalation'], ['Primary Actor', 'System Administrator'], ['Preconditions', 'User is authenticated with role system_admin.'], ['Trigger', 'Administrator navigates to /admin/audit-logs.'], ['Main Success Scenario', '1. System fetches chronological audit log records from audit_logs collection.\n2. System displays tabular log feed showing timestamp, actor ID, action code, target entity, and IP address.\n3. Administrator filters logs by action code (e.g., AUTH_REPLAY_DETECTED or SLA_BREACH).\n4. Administrator clicks on a log entry to inspect full JSON before/after state diff.\n5. Administrator identifies stalled ticket and clicks Trigger Manual Escalation.\n6. Backend dispatches priority alert to responsible Hall Council and logs manual escalation event.'], ['Extensions / Alternative Flows', '1a. Database connectivity loss: System displays retry banner with diagnostic error.'], ['Postconditions', 'Audit trail verified; security compliance and accountability enforced.']]}], 'algorithms': [{'title': 'Algorithm 3.1: Scoped Role-Based Authorization Middleware (requireRoleAndHall)', 'caption': 'Listing 3.1: Pseudocode for Scoped Role and Hall Authorization Middleware', 'code': "Algorithm requireRoleAndHall(allowedRoles, enforceHallMatch):\n  Input: req (HTTPRequest), res (HTTPResponse), next (MiddlewareCallback)\n  Output: Execution granted to next handler, or HTTP error response\n  1:  authHeader <- req.headers['authorization']\n  2:  IF authHeader is NULL OR NOT authHeader.startsWith('Bearer ') THEN\n  3:      RETURN res.status(401).json({ error: 'Authentication token missing' })\n  4:  END IF\n  5:  token <- authHeader.split(' ')[1]\n  6:  TRY\n  7:      decodedUser <- verifyJwt(token, JWT_SECRET)\n  8:      req.user <- decodedUser\n  9:  CATCH TokenExpiredError\n 10:      RETURN res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired', code: 'TOKEN_EXPIRED' })\n 11:  CATCH JsonWebTokenError\n 12:      RETURN res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid token' })\n 13:  END TRY\n 14:  IF allowedRoles NOT CONTAINS req.user.role THEN\n 15:      RETURN res.status(403).json({ error: 'Insufficient role permissions' })\n 16:  END IF\n 17:  IF enforceHallMatch IS TRUE AND req.user.role IN ['hall_manager', 'maintenance'] THEN\n 18:      targetHallId <- req.params.hallId OR req.body.residence\n 19:      IF targetHallId is NULL AND req.params.issueId IS NOT NULL THEN\n 20:          targetIssue <- findIssueById(req.params.issueId)\n 21:          targetHallId <- targetIssue.residence\n 22:      END IF\n 23:      IF targetHallId != req.user.residence THEN\n 24:          RETURN res.status(403).json({ error: 'Access denied: Hall boundary mismatch' })\n 25:      END IF\n 26:  END IF\n 27:  EXECUTE next()\nEnd Algorithm"}, {'title': 'Algorithm 3.2: State Transition Engine and Invariant Verification (transitionIssueState)', 'caption': 'Listing 3.2: Pseudocode for Issue Lifecycle State Transition Engine', 'code': "Algorithm transitionIssueState(issueId, targetState, actorUser, metadata):\n  Input: issueId (ObjectID), targetState (Enum), actorUser (User), metadata (Object)\n  Output: updatedIssue (Issue) or Exception\n  1:  issue <- findIssueById(issueId)\n  2:  IF issue IS NULL THEN THROW NotFoundException('Issue does not exist') END IF\n  3:  currentState <- issue.status\n  4:  VALID_TRANSITIONS <- {\n        'submitted':    ['acknowledged', 'rejected'],\n        'acknowledged': ['in_progress', 'resolved', 'rejected'],\n        'in_progress':  ['resolved'],\n        'resolved':     ['reopened', 'closed'],\n        'reopened':     ['in_progress', 'resolved', 'acknowledged'],\n        'rejected':     [],\n        'closed':       []\n      }\n  5:  IF targetState NOT IN VALID_TRANSITIONS[currentState] THEN\n  6:      THROW InvalidStateTransitionException('Illegal transition from ' + currentState + ' to ' + targetState)\n  7:  END IF\n  8:  IF targetState == 'resolved' THEN\n  9:      issue.resolvedAt <- getCurrentTimestamp()\n 10:      issue.disputeWindowClosesAt <- getCurrentTimestamp() + (48 * 3600 * 1000)\n 11:      issue.resolutionNotes <- metadata.notes\n 12:  ELSE IF targetState == 'closed' THEN\n 13:      issue.closedAt <- getCurrentTimestamp()\n 14:  ELSE IF targetState == 'rejected' THEN\n 15:      IF metadata.rejectionReason IS NULL OR length(metadata.rejectionReason) < 5 THEN\n 16:          THROW ValidationException('Rejection reason is required')\n 17:      END IF\n 18:      issue.rejectionReason <- metadata.rejectionReason\n 19:  END IF\n 20:  issue.status <- targetState\n 21:  issue.updatedAt <- getCurrentTimestamp()\n 22:  save(issue)\n 23:  createIssueEvent(issueId, currentState, targetState, actorUser._id, metadata.notes)\n 24:  dispatchNotification(issue, targetState, actorUser)\n 25:  RETURN issue\nEnd Algorithm"}, {'title': 'Algorithm 3.3: Automated SLA Overdue Escalation Daemon', 'caption': 'Listing 3.3: Pseudocode for Background SLA Overdue Escalation Daemon', 'code': "Algorithm runOverdueTicketEscalationDaemon():\n  Input: None (Scheduled every 15 minutes by node-cron: '*/15 * * * *')\n  Output: Number of escalated tickets\n  1:  currentTime <- getCurrentTimestamp()\n  2:  SLA_THRESHOLDS <- { 'urgent': 12, 'high': 24, 'medium': 48, 'low': 96 } // Hours\n  3:  activeTickets <- findIssues({\n        status: { $in: ['submitted', 'acknowledged', 'in_progress', 'reopened'] },\n        isOverdue: false\n      })\n  4:  escalatedCount <- 0\n  5:  FOR EACH ticket IN activeTickets DO\n  6:      allowedDurationHours <- SLA_THRESHOLDS[ticket.priority]\n  7:      elapsedHours <- (currentTime - ticket.createdAt) / (1000 * 3600)\n  8:      IF elapsedHours > allowedDurationHours THEN\n  9:          ticket.isOverdue <- TRUE\n 10:          save(ticket)\n 11:          createAuditLog('SLA_BREACH', ticket._id, 'System Cron', 'Ticket exceeded ' + allowedDurationHours + 'h')\n 12:          dispatchUrgentManagerAlert(ticket.residence, ticket)\n 13:          escalatedCount <- escalatedCount + 1\n 14:      END IF\n 15:  END FOR\n 16:  LOG('Escalation daemon completed. Tickets escalated: ' + escalatedCount)\n 17:  RETURN escalatedCount\nEnd Algorithm"}, {'title': 'Algorithm 3.4: Cryptographic Refresh Token Rotation and Replay Detection', 'caption': 'Listing 3.4: Pseudocode for Dual-Token Rotation and Replay Detection Engine', 'code': 'Algorithm rotateRefreshToken(incomingCookieToken, clientIp, userAgent):\n  Input: incomingCookieToken (String), clientIp (String), userAgent (String)\n  Output: newAccessToken (JWT), newRefreshToken (String) or 401 Unauthorized\n  1:  IF incomingCookieToken IS NULL THEN RETURN 401 Unauthorized END IF\n  2:  tokenHash <- sha256(incomingCookieToken)\n  3:  storedSession <- findRefreshToken({ tokenHash: tokenHash })\n  4:  IF storedSession IS NULL THEN\n  5:      RETURN 401 Unauthorized("Invalid session")\n  6:  END IF\n  7:  IF storedSession.isRevoked IS TRUE THEN\n  8:      // Replay attack detected: Compromised token reused!\n  9:      revokeAllUserSessions(storedSession.user)\n 10:      createAuditLog("AUTH_REPLAY_DETECTED", storedSession.user, clientIp, "All sessions invalidated")\n 11:      RETURN 401 Unauthorized("Security breach detected. All sessions revoked.")\n 12:  END IF\n 13:  IF storedSession.expiresAt < getCurrentTimestamp() THEN\n 14:      RETURN 401 Unauthorized("Session expired")\n 15:  END IF\n 16:  storedSession.isRevoked <- TRUE\n 17:  save(storedSession)\n 18:  user <- findUserById(storedSession.user)\n 19:  newAccessToken <- generateJwt({ id: user._id, role: user.role, residence: user.residence }, 15 * 60)\n 20:  rawNewRefreshToken <- generateSecureRandomBytes(48)\n 21:  newHash <- sha256(rawNewRefreshToken)\n 22:  createRefreshTokenRecord({ tokenHash: newHash, user: user._id, expiresAt: now() + 7 days, clientIp })\n 23:  RETURN { newAccessToken, rawNewRefreshToken }\nEnd Algorithm'}, {'title': 'Algorithm 3.5: Mean Time to Repair (MTTR) and Resolution Rate Aggregation', 'caption': 'Listing 3.5: Pseudocode for Cross-Hall Facility Metrics Aggregation Pipeline', 'code': 'Algorithm calculateHallMetrics(startDate, endDate):\n  Input: startDate (Date), endDate (Date)\n  Output: Array of HallMetrics objects containing MTTR, MTTA, and Resolution Rates\n  1:  pipeline <- [\n        { : { createdAt: { : startDate, : endDate } } },\n        { : {\n            _id: "",\n            totalIssues: { : 1 },\n            resolvedCount: { : { : [{ : ["0", ["resolved", "closed"]] }, 1, 0] } },\n            totalRepairTimeMs: { : {\n              : [\n                { : ["", { : ["", ""]] } },\n                { : ["", ""] },\n                0\n              ]\n            }},\n            resolvedWithTiming: { : { : ["", 1, 0] } }\n          }\n        },\n        { : { from: "residences", localField: "_id", foreignField: "_id", as: "hall" } },\n        { : "" }\n      ]\n  2:  aggregatedResults <- executeMongoAggregate("issues", pipeline)\n  3:  outputList <- []\n  4:  FOR EACH record IN aggregatedResults DO\n  5:      resolutionRate <- (record.resolvedCount / record.totalIssues) * 100\n  6:      mttrHours <- record.resolvedWithTiming > 0 ? (record.totalRepairTimeMs / record.resolvedWithTiming) / (3600 * 1000) : 0\n  7:      outputList.append({\n            hallName: record.hall.name,\n            hallCode: record.hall.code,\n            totalTickets: record.totalIssues,\n            resolvedTickets: record.resolvedCount,\n            resolutionRatePercent: round(resolutionRate, 1),\n            meanTimeToRepairHours: round(mttrHours, 1)\n          })\n  8:  END FOR\n  9:  RETURN sortBy(outputList, "meanTimeToRepairHours", ASCENDING)\nEnd Algorithm'}, {'title': 'Algorithm 3.6: Multi-Criteria Issue Search and Triage Filtering Engine', 'caption': 'Listing 3.6: Pseudocode for Dynamic Multi-Criteria Issue Filtering Engine', 'code': 'Algorithm filterIssueQueue(user, queryParams):\n  Input: user (User), queryParams (Object: status, category, priority, search, page, limit)\n  Output: PaginatedResult (tickets Array, totalCount Number, totalPages Number)\n  1:  filterConditions <- {}\n  2:  // Enforce role-based tenant isolation\n  3:  IF user.role == "student" THEN\n  4:      filterConditions.reporter <- user._id\n  5:  ELSE IF user.role IN ["hall_manager", "maintenance"] THEN\n  6:      filterConditions.residence <- user.residence\n  7:      IF user.role == "maintenance" AND queryParams.onlyAssigned == TRUE THEN\n  8:          filterConditions.assignedTo <- user._id\n  9:      END IF\n 10:  END IF\n 11:  // Apply dynamic client query parameters\n 12:  IF queryParams.status AND queryParams.status != "all" THEN\n 13:      filterConditions.status <- queryParams.status\n 14:  END IF\n 15:  IF queryParams.category AND queryParams.category != "all" THEN\n 16:      filterConditions.category <- queryParams.category\n 17:  END IF\n 18:  IF queryParams.priority AND queryParams.priority != "all" THEN\n 19:      filterConditions.priority <- queryParams.priority\n 20:  END IF\n 21:  IF queryParams.search AND length(queryParams.search) > 0 THEN\n 22:      regexPattern <- new Regex(queryParams.search, "i")\n 23:      filterConditions. <- [\n            { ticketNumber: regexPattern },\n            { title: regexPattern },\n            { "location.room": regexPattern }\n          ]\n 24:  END IF\n 25:  skipCount <- (queryParams.page - 1) * queryParams.limit\n 26:  totalCount <- countDocuments("issues", filterConditions)\n 27:  tickets <- findIssues("issues", filterConditions, { createdAt: -1 }, skipCount, queryParams.limit)\n 28:  RETURN { tickets, totalCount, totalPages: ceil(totalCount / queryParams.limit) }\nEnd Algorithm'}]}, {'num': '3.7', 'title': 'Hardware and Software Specifications', 'paragraphs': ['To ensure predictable system performance, reliability, and security across development, deployment, and client execution environments, the hardware and software specifications governing HostelFix are formalized below:'], 'specs_table': {'caption': 'Table 3.14: Comprehensive Hardware and Software Environment Specifications', 'headers': ['Environment Tier', 'Component / Specification', 'Minimum Requirement', 'Recommended / Tested Configuration'], 'rows': [['Development', 'Host Processor', 'Apple Silicon M1 / Intel Core i5 (Quad-core)', 'Apple M2 Pro (10-core CPU), 16GB Unified RAM'], ['Development', 'Host Memory (RAM)', '8 GB DDR4', '16 GB Unified Memory'], ['Development', 'Storage Capacity', '256 GB Solid State Drive (SSD)', '512 GB NVMe SSD'], ['Development', 'Operating System', 'macOS Sonoma 14 / Ubuntu 22.04 LTS / Win 11', 'macOS Sonoma 14.5 / Darwin Kernel 23.5'], ['Development', 'Runtime Environment', 'Node.js v20.10.0 LTS', 'Node.js v20.17.0 LTS with PNPM v9.9.0'], ['Development', 'Database Instance', 'MongoDB Community Server v7.0', 'MongoDB Community v7.0.12 (Local) + Atlas Cloud'], ['Production Server', 'Virtual Compute (vCPU)', '2 vCPU Compute Units', '4 vCPU Dedicated High-Performance Compute'], ['Production Server', 'System Memory', '4 GB RAM', '8 GB DDR4 ECC RAM'], ['Production Server', 'Storage System', '40 GB NVMe Cloud Storage', '80 GB High-IOPS Cloud Storage with daily backups'], ['Production Server', 'Operating System', 'Ubuntu Linux 22.04 LTS (Jammy Jellyfish)', 'Ubuntu Linux 24.04 LTS x86_64'], ['Production Server', 'Process Supervisor', 'Node.js Direct Process', 'PM2 Runtime in Cluster Mode (max instances)'], ['Production Server', 'Web Server / Proxy', 'Nginx v1.18', 'Nginx v1.24 with Brotli compression & TLS 1.3'], ['Client Device', 'Desktop Hardware', 'Dual-core CPU, 4GB RAM, 1366x768 Display', 'Intel Core i5 / Apple M-series, 8GB RAM, 1080p'], ['Client Device', 'Mobile Hardware', 'ARM Quad-core, 2GB RAM, 375x667 Display', 'Modern 4G/5G Smartphone, 4GB RAM, 1080x2400'], ['Client Software', 'Web Browser Support', 'Google Chrome 110+, Safari 16+, Firefox 110+', 'Latest Evergreen Chrome, Safari iOS, Firefox, Edge']]}}]}
